    {
      "id": "values",
      "title_zh": "牌点",
      "title_en": "Card Values",
      "source_zh": "编辑后的讲义 Blackjack Training",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "assets/cards_clean.png",
          "alt": "讲义牌点图：2 到 9 按面值，10、J、Q、K 是 10，A 是 1 或 11"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "2 到 9 按点数。10、J、Q、K 都是 10。A 是 1 或 11。"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "en": "Soft Hands: When an ace in the dealers/players hand can be counted as 11 or 1.",
          "zh": "软牌：这手牌里的 A 可以算 11，也可以算 1。"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "例子：Ace and a 4；Ace, 4 and a 3；Ace and a 9。软牌再补一张不会马上爆，因为 A 可以改算 1。"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "en": "Hard hands have no varying Ace value.",
          "zh": "硬牌：A 的点数不能再变。"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "没有 A，或者 A 算 11 会爆所以只能算 1。例子：Ace, 5 and an 8；10 and a 7；Ace, 3 and a Jack。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "splits",
      "title_zh": "分牌",
      "title_en": "Splits",
      "source_zh": "编辑后的讲义 Blackjack Training",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "en": "A player can split their first two cards that are of equal value.",
          "zh": "前两张点数相同才能分。"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "必须再放一份和原注相同的注。最多分 3 次，一共 4 手。A 只能分一次，每手只给 1 张。分牌后可以加倍，但分开的 A 不能加倍。"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "en": "All double down bets must be moved to the right side of the original bet.",
          "zh": "讲义把这句话印在分牌这一节：所有加倍的注都要挪到原注的右侧。"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "这句按这版讲义执行。加倍那一节也写：加倍的筹码放在原注右侧。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "doubles",
      "title_zh": "加倍",
      "title_en": "Doubling Down",
      "source_zh": "编辑后的讲义 Blackjack Training",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "任意两张都可以加倍，blackjack 除外。加倍的筹码放到原注右侧。金额可以到原注为止，不能超过。少于原注时，要向客人确认：doubling down for less。"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "不常见的加倍要喊出来。讲义的例子是 doubling down on a hard 12。两张是对子、既可能分也可能加倍时，先问是 split 还是 double down。"
        },
        {
          "type": "calls",
          "audio_ids": [
            "d-double-less",
            "d-double-hard-12",
            "d-split-or-double"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
